# ── Rust ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
target_cli/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace produces a binary (the editor), and a
# locked dependency set is what makes a build reproducible for everyone.

# ── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.env
.env.local

# ── Build & profiling artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.profraw
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
/dist/

# ── Third-party rigs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rigs authored in other tools, and anything converted from them. Converting a
# file does not relicense the art inside it, so these stay local however they
# arrived. Committed samples are the generated ones (walker.ankh, minimal.ankh).
/samples/skf/
/samples/skellina.ankh
/samples/spineboy*.ankh
/samples/*_imported.ankh
/samples/*_reimported.ankh
# Local one-off converters for foreign rigs. Not product code, and they only
# exist while a specific import is being chased.
/formats/examples/import_skf_once.rs
/formats/examples/import_spine_once.rs
/formats/examples/verify_once.rs
/preview.png

# ── Scratch output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exported renders and test rigs written while trying things out. Real sample
# projects live in samples/ and are committed.
/out/
/scratch/
*.mp4
*.webm
/formats/examples/probe_once.rs
